<title>GERMANY: Mercedes says resumes Spanish production.</title>
<headline>Mercedes says resumes Spanish production.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Mercedes-Benz AG said on Thursday that it had resumed production at two Spanish factories after truck drivers in Spain said on Wednesday they would end their strike.</p>
<p>&quot;The production lines in Spain are running again,&quot; a Mercedes spokesman said.</p>
<p>Mercedes said production of about 1,000 of its V-Class transporters was affected by the week-long stoppage in production at a plant in Vitoria and also at a parts production plant in Barcelona.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
